<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chaubise Rajya</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chaubise Rajya, the 'twenty-four kingdoms', were a group of small hill principalities in the Gandaki region of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, many ruled by dynasties claiming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> descent. Palpa, Tanahun and Lamjung were among the strongest. In the 18th century the Gorkha kingdom, which had grown from them, conquered them during the unification of Nepal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chaubise-rajya.jpg" alt="Chaubise Rajya" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CAPTAIN MEDUSA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prithvi_Narayan_Shah_1960_(restoration).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
